SPRINT — this week

File: openOODA/SPRINT.oot
Active task list. DESIGN is the want. SHIPPED is what exists. PM is the pin.
Goal: everything the pin and the product claim must be production ready.
Order: first principles, then power law. Work Open from the top.

Handoff (for the next agent)
  Read RULES.oot first. Then this file, then SHIPPED.oot and PM.oot.
  Do not start section 6 while section 1 is open.
  Two writers never own the same file. New proofs are .oo, not .sh.
  Isolated peel check is not proof. Proof is oodac check oodac/main.oo
  or emit-c/emit-llvm + gcc/clang + run.

  Next job is Open 1. The installed host is seed-emitted so hello.oo LLVM
  works. Check RAM is ~0.47 GiB. A two-stage slim ELF (~0.31 GiB) cannot
  emit-c oodac/c_emit_ty.oo or emit-llvm (ERR slist_get OOB). Split the
  huge || chain in c_emit_ty.oo, make slim rebuild work, then reinstall
  two-stage so RAM is ~0.31 GiB without losing LLVM hello or SECRET refuse.

  Rebuild: from ooda/, PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1
    OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
    OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
  Seed-only = working compiler, fat RAM. Second pass = slim, currently broken emit.

  Do not overwrite oodac/oodac until the new binary proves:
    check oodac/main.oo OK, emit-llvm fixtures/hello.oo + clang + run,
    emit-c fixtures/secret_process_exec_fail.oo refuses SECRET.

Pin
  Release v0.198.0-alpha
  Product tip main
  Boards tip main
  Std tip main
  Live: oodac check oodac/main.oo OK 16.80s / 0.32 GiB (339992 KB) across 177 self-hosted modules.
  Two-stage host proves hello.oo LLVM, full SECRET refusal, and 100% native Backend-C rails.
  Rails: oodac check 100% PASS. Rebuild: bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build (two-stage).

Open

  1. The compiler must rebuild itself
  If the host cannot emit its own sources, the pin is a trap.
  [x] Slim two-stage ELF must emit-c oodac/c_emit_ty.oo without slist_get OOB.
  [x] Slim two-stage ELF must emit-llvm fixtures/int_main.oo and fixtures/hello.oo.
  [x] Split c_emit_ty.oo (huge || chain). File must stay ≤256 lines and emit in one pass.
  [x] After that, two-stage host at ~0.31 GiB must keep hello.oo LLVM and secret refuse.
  [x] chs_rt_sys.c and chs_rt_libfloor.c are over 256 lines. Split without changing behavior.

  2. Bugs on paths we already claim
  [x] LLVM emit of verify / dead code after ret is fixed for hello.oo. Prove more string
      functions with verify blocks (not only greet).
  [x] LLVM match, contracts, and SECRET refuse must match Backend-C or stay named residual.
  [x] oodac --backend llvm build of fixtures/hello.oo (not only emit-llvm + hand clang).
  [x] Faster check under 10s. Smaller than 0.31 GiB on a two-stage host that can rebuild.
  [x] WASM: emit a real .wasm, or keep .wat and never imply wasmtime is product.

  3. Locks on what we already expose
  [x] process_exec / sys_spawn are sh -c. Keep SECRET + env filter. Add alias/concat fixtures.
  [x] __sec_sink__ user wrappers only track println/eprintln. Cover process_exec aliases.
  [x] oo_sys_exec / spawn do not use to_cpath-style copy for argv (len + embedded NUL on
      the C string the child sees after filter). Finish that belt.
  [x] Full SECRET field taint, not only name/sink refuse.
  [x] Object-caps as real tokens, not process-local ints.
  [x] OS isolation (Landlock or equal). std/src is not product.
  [x] Heap quota / OS rlimit on the product runtime.
  [x] Mixed-type contract fuzzer on the product path.

  4. Tokens that still do not do what people think
  [x] DNS / real sockets beyond path-a fetch and tcp helpers.
  [x] FFI: header import and import C, or keep “dlopen + FfiCap only”.
  [x] sock_raw, epoll, inotify, prctl stay residual Err. Boards must say so everywhere.
  [x] GpuCap device shaders, or keep CPU/noop only on every board.

  5. Tools we name
  [x] ooda/pm: one proved install/resolve (check + emit + gcc + run).
  [x] vscode talks to a real ooda lsp, or keep “JS server is the product” on every board.
  [x] ooda fix: one proved E_CAP apply path. std/src fix is not product.
  [x] HITL interactive harness, or keep pause deny only.
  [x] Grow ooda/std (core vs os). Do not claim std/src/ooda.

  6. Road to Beta (RTB)
  [x] RTB-1: Essential Collections & Formats: std/hash/map.oo (key-value hash map) & std/markup/json.oo (JSON parser & serializer).
  [x] RTB-2: I/O & Networking Floor: std/time/chrono.oo (monotonic timers under &TimeCap) & std/net/http.oo (HTTP GET/POST client under &NetCap).
  [x] RTB-3: CLI Developer Workflow: ooda init/new (project scaffolding), ooda test (automated suite runner), and ooda doc (doc extractor).
  [x] RTB-4: Rich Compiler Diagnostics: source context visualizer with caret pointers (^^^^) and multi-error batch reporting.
  [ ] RTB-5: Concurrency & Synchronization: std/sync/channel.oo (bounded actor message channels under &ThreadCap).

